„­bible_version£KJV¤book+§chapter¨sections˜…¤book+§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙKBut a certain man named Ananias, with Sapphira his wife, sold a possession,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€and kept back part of the price, his wife also being privy to it, and brought a certain part, and laid it at the apostles' feet.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„But Peter said, Ananias, why hath Satan filled thine heart to lie to the Holy Ghost, and to keep back part of the price of the land?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ½Whiles it remained, was it not thine own? and after it was sold, was it not in thine own power? why hast thou conceived this thing in thine heart? thou hast not lied unto men, but unto God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙzAnd Ananias hearing these words fell down, and gave up the ghost: and great fear came on all them that heard these things.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙKAnd the young men arose, wound him up, and carried him out, and buried him.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book+§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙcAnd it was about the space of three hours after, when his wife, not knowing what was done, came in.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjAnd Peter answered unto her, Tell me whether ye sold the land for so much? And she said, Yea, for so much.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÃThen Peter said unto her, How is it that ye have agreed together to tempt the Spirit of the Lord? behold, the feet of them which have buried thy husband are at the door, and shall carry thee out.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
