„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙPAnd great fear came upon all the church, and upon as many as heard these things.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book+§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd by the hands of the apostles were many signs and wonders wrought among the people; (and they were all with one accord in Solomon's porch.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQAnd of the rest durst no man join himself to them: but the people magnified them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQAnd believers were the more added to the Lord, multitudes both of men and women.)¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ®Insomuch that they brought forth the sick into the streets, and laid them on beds and couches, that at the least the shadow of Peter passing by might overshadow some of them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ®There came also a multitude out of the cities round about unto Jerusalem, bringing sick folks, and them which were vexed with unclean spirits: and they were healed every one.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book+§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†Then the high priest rose up, and all they that were with him, (which is the sect of the Sadducees,) and were filled with indignation,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHand laid their hands on the apostles, and put them in the common prison.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]But the angel of the Lord by night opened the prison doors, and brought them forth, and said,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙKGo, stand and speak in the temple to the people all the words of this life.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book+§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚAnd when they heard that, they entered into the temple early in the morning, and taught. But the high priest came, and they that were with him, and called the council together, and all the senate of the children of Israel, and sent to the prison to have them brought.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVBut when the officers came, and found them not in the prison, they returned, and told,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙšsaying, The prison truly found we shut with all safety, and the keepers standing without before the doors: but when we had opened, we found no man within.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNow when the high priest and the captain of the temple and the chief priests heard these things, they doubted of them whereunto this would grow.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙThen came one and told them, saying, Behold, the men whom ye put in prison are standing in the temple, and teaching the people.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŠThen went the captain with the officers, and brought them without violence: for they feared the people, lest they should have been stoned.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book+§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse ¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaAnd when they had brought them, they set them before the council: and the high priest asked them,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¶saying, Did not we straitly command you that ye should not teach in this name? and, behold, ye have filled Jerusalem with your doctrine, and intend to bring this man's blood upon us.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙZThen Peter and the other apostles answered and said, We ought to obey God rather than men.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙJThe God of our fathers raised up Jesus, whom ye slew and hanged on a tree.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHim hath God exalted with his right hand to be a Prince and a Saviour, for to give repentance to Israel, and forgiveness of sins.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsAnd we are his witnesses of these things; and so is also the Holy Ghost, whom God hath given to them that obey him.¦layout ªlast_verse …¤book+§chapter«first_verse!ªlast_verse'¦verses—„¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙPWhen they heard that, they were cut to the heart, and took counsel to slay them.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¸Then stood there up one in the council, a Pharisee, named Gamaliel, a doctor of the law, had in reputation among all the people, and commanded to put the apostles forth a little space;¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙiand said unto them, Ye men of Israel, take heed to yourselves what ye intend to do as touching these men.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙİFor before these days rose up Theudas, boasting himself to be somebody; to whom a number of men, about four hundred, joined themselves: who was slain; and all, as many as obeyed him, were scattered, and brought to nought.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ®After this man rose up Judas of Galilee in the days of the taxing, and drew away much people after him: he also perished; and all, even as many as obeyed him, were dispersed.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡And now I say unto you, Refrain from these men, and let them alone: for if this counsel or this work be of men, it will come to nought:¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^but if it be of God, ye cannot overthrow it; lest haply ye be found even to fight against God.¦layout ªlast_verse'…¤book+§chapter«first_verse(ªlast_verse*¦verses“„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ And to him they agreed: and when they had called the apostles, and beaten them, they commanded that they should not speak in the name of Jesus, and let them go.¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyAnd they departed from the presence of the council, rejoicing that they were counted worthy to suffer shame for his name.¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^And daily in the temple, and in every house, they ceased not to teach and preach Jesus Christ.¦layout ªlast_verse*